  "flags_for_jon": [
    "No scene_art_notes exist for Part 1 (the part sheet has no such field), so the pictures' look comes from part-01's \"place\" line and the master: honey-gold hearth light indoors, low gold then orange sun on the road, then night blue with stars and the lantern's tiny blue glow. Suggest prompt 1c add a scene_art_notes field so all five Part 1 chapters draw from one note.",
    "Canon §8's picture-book layout (N2) shows a \"Last time\" line on the picture-book page. 1e's schema has no field for it and the first picture must start with the legend slot, so no \"Last time\" line is in the picture text; suggest the app shows the master's opening_block.last_time above picture 1, as the N2 layout does.",
    "Kit wording: 1e says the \"For the youngest\" prompt sits at the youngest's act picture, but the schema nests it in pause_and_ask_simple with the Pause & ask picture's number (and the checker wants that). Kept as the schema. The talk prompt (\"What color is the little flame now?\") answers the same at pictures 8 and 9, since the flame is a blue bead in both.",
    "The master marks two youngest acts: \"Please\" as the flame is given (p3) and \"Big stone!\" at the crisis (p25). The youngest_act role goes to \"Big stone!\" (picture 9, p25), the act that changes what happens; \"Please\" has its own picture (2). The key act is the eldest's, so the checker confirms this pin by judgment.",
    "Simplified for one speaker a picture and four sentences at most. The eldest's middle way now comes before the youngest's act, in picture 8, in short words (\"The answer came: 'Rushing on is silly. Stopping is brave.'\"), so the reasoning comes before the deed. Picture 11 is the lantern set down, the wall (the middle child helps; the youngest is asleep) and Ember's clue as a friendly one (\"Someone I know walked this road tonight,\" with a happy swish of her tail). The last picture now opens on the warm anchor from the master, the grandparent knitting \"by a fire that stayed awake\", then the youngest asleep in Ember's tail and the canon's hook, so a 3-year-old hearing only this telling ends on home and sleep, not on someone walking the road. Left out of the words (kept in the master): Ember's fib-sneeze, the old law of the road, \"That is my tail, and I should like it back\", \"Who?\" and \"Sleep now.\"",
    "The favorite-animal slot in the jar default (jar.p3) is neither named in picture 6's words nor drawn, so a family's own favorite never contradicts the picture. Drawing a family's favorite would need a Tier C picture.",
